consumer loans, such as motor vehicle, home improvement, home equity, signature loans, and small personal credit lines, as well as issuance of trust preferred securities. QCR Holdings, Inc. was incorporated in 1993 and is headquartered in Moline, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Todd A. Gipple CPA | President, CEO & Director | Age 61 | Compensation: $1.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $364K ranks in the below the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 12%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $349K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $3K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (5/10).","financial_summary":["QCR Holdings, Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $1.6B market cap on $370M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -0% over the past three years and +12% annually across the full decade \u2014 essentially flat, and a business treading water is rarely a path to compounding.","Returns on capital run at 14% against a 9% cost of capital, a 5-point spread that creates value, though narrow enough that competitive pressure could close it.","The business throws off $354M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 96 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.31\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.6\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.5%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 3.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.3) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 71% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Returns on capital have been remarkably steady for 5 years \u2014 durability is the real test of a moat","24 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Understanding Momentum Shifts in (QCRH)","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/12/Understanding_Momentum_Shifts_in_QCRH_110326050801_1793700481.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793700481.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"QCR Holdings (QCRH) Record EPS Puts Its Undervalued Narrative Back In Focus","source":"simplywall.st","